A||||28||JohnnyK||Unquenchable need for speed!!||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-19-2000||11:21 PM||||Ok, I am planning on getting a new car, and I want it to be damn fast, yet cheap. Should I get a 70's muscle car, or an 80's car? I wanna have it amazingly fast. I was talking to some mustang people and they said I would be disappointed with the performance of the 429's and what not compared to modern cars. I thought if I got something like a charger, I could basically fly and destroy any car on the road? What gives? Someone fill me in!||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||12-20-2000||12:05 AM||||Put a big engine into your Fiero !!!!!!!!||||reg||7
Z||000002||Sleeper||12-20-2000||12:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Ok, I am planning on getting a new car, and I want it to be damn fast, yet cheap.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>wanna go fast=cheap...I don't think so.<P>wanna go fast=lots of money...if you REALLY wanna go fast you're going to have to fork out the bucks. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||12-20-2000||02:37 AM||||Faster than anything on the road...<P>You also have to consider do you want to go fast in a straight line? Or do you actually want it to turn?<P>Even with a beefed up suspension, a steel hulk of a legendary Hemi Charger will never out maneuver a beefed up Fiero. <P>Fast and cheap? Kinda like wanting money but not have to work for it. Nice, but still a dream. And there will ALWAYS be someone faster than you.<P>Don't get a car just because its fast, get it something that you can enjoy. I doubt if anybody got a Fiero because it could go fast.||||reg||5
Z||000004||GT Bastard||12-20-2000||08:23 AM||||Some people may not agree with me, but I'd go with a Chrysler turbo 4cyl.  They even come in intercooled flavors.  They put them in all sorts of cars... Omni GLH-T, Shadow CSX, Acclaim, Daytona, Charger, 84-86 Laser. They're cheap, and they can easily be tweaked.  I've done some serious reasearch on these cars and I'm working on getting an intercooled Daytona soon... Read up on the extra injector and bleed mods.  Bleed the boost to 15psi, add that injector, and slap an intercooler on that bad boy.  There's a ton of websites with people in the 13's with just those mods and mild weight reduction.  Hell, the 2.5 Turbo Minivan is in the 13's(he's got lots more than that though...)<BR> <A HREF="http://idt.net/~gdonovan/turbo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://idt.net/~gdonovan/turbo.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.turbogearhead.com/index2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turbogearhead.com/index2.htm</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||12-20-2000||08:48 AM||||jeff.. when you do get one.. let me know i'll see if i can't get ya a REAL boost controller... Profec-B. <P>you wanna be STOOPID quick (0-60 in 4)or STOOPID fast(170mph)? a Starion / Conquest are cheap and FAST.. EASY to make CRAZY fast. and there are lots of parts out there for them. or 86.5-93 Supra Turbo. those are cheap and fast you pick up an 87 (around here) for 4500 with 100k on it... you cna EASILY get 200K out of the motor. and you can get CRAZY HP out of that sweet straight six...  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Supra.jpg">   <P>380hp and 414lbft!!! on a STOCK motor.. with a little tuning and a few bolt ons!<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||12-20-2000||09:10 AM||||That much HP on what motor?? I was thinking of getting a muscle car of some form, but doing some adjustments to it.. Lowering, etc. You guys didn't answer my question though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Are muscle cars (particularly Mustangs and Chargers) faster than cars nowadays? They put out 375 HP, so I assume they would be? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||12-20-2000||09:18 AM||||My pick for damn fast + cheap would be a rusty 5-liter Mustang.  Gotta be rusty or it won't be cheap...a good-running 5.0 with body cancer shouldn't run more than $2000.  Go for the '86 and newer (fuel-injected) if you can, but don't turn your nose up at a good-running '84 or '85.<P>I'd forget '70s muscle cars - they aren't cheap anymore.  Plus, as bad as 5.0 Mustang brakes are, they're much better than '70s brakes.  I've owned a '71 Charger and a '72 Duster.  Trust me!||||reg||1
Z||000008||p4n1c||12-20-2000||11:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT Bastard:<BR><B>Some people may not agree with me, but I'd go with a Chrysler turbo 4cyl.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with you fully.  A friend of mine had an '86 base model 4-door 2.2l turbo Shadow(They seem rare to me, all the turbo Shadows I see are 2-door ESs).  The thing flew even with the timing bad, sure it spit and sputtered in first and then the turbo kicked in, it would push us back in our seat at WOT.<P>Sadly too many problems started popping up, with the previous owner not taking care of the car. Bad maintenance + lots of miles on a 14 year old 4-cyl starts to add up on it. =]  He sold it and got a '90 Corsica LT for 400 bucks. lol.||||reg||10
Z||000009||BBBAD GT||12-20-2000||11:29 AM||||I'd go late model if I were you.  <P>My first choice (of course) would be a 87-93 5.0.  My Stang is turning low 11's (should be mid 10's with the MPH), and was driven to the track two hours and back. I regularly drive it to work (1/2 hr drive each way).  I've also poured my heart and soul into it, but you can buy similar turnkey stangs, there are tons out there (just look on ebay).<P>The LS1 Fbody's with N2O are tuning low 12's/high 11's bone stock.  I really don't think early muscle cars can touch that and still be driveable.  <P>Also, check insurance rates before you buy, that might make your decision easier.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||12-20-2000||12:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B> Are muscle cars (particularly Mustangs and Chargers) faster than cars nowadays? They put out 375 HP, so I assume they would be? Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First you have to consider the HP ratings in the 60's/70's were gross HP ratings estimated by the manufacturer.  Sometimes that number is high, sometimes low. HP ratings nowadays are far more uniform. The exception would be Japanese spec cars, which according to the manufacturers, don't make over 275 HP (wink, wink) due to an agreement in the industry to limit output.<P>I guess the equation that you are looking for is s=&gt;$. Speed for less cash. What is your definition of cheap? Musclecars don't fit in my factoring of that equation. They are great nostalgia mobiles, but are from from being the affordable rides they were back in the oil crisis days. I would go along with the mini hot-rod idea. The Shelby GLHS or Mitsubishi Colt turbo were both screamers back in the day. Or if you don't mind having a project, I have a slightly rumpled Mazda 323 GTX (turbo 16v 1.6 intercooled, AWD) for sale- CHEAP! Hate to say it but this car is much quicker then my Fiero GT, and with minor turbo mods is capable of 180 hp without lifting the valve cover.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JBGehling||12-20-2000||12:07 PM||||Get a 90's Nissan 300ZX for about $10,000 put about $10,000 more dollars in it and you've got 780 HP...<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000012||WampusCat||12-20-2000||12:14 PM||||If you can find an older Miata for $5000, put a Flyin' Miata II turbo on for $4800 and you have 240 rear wheel hp in a 2300 pound car.  Those 323's have lots of aftermarket stuff too.  A mustang SVO or thumderbird turbo couple 2.3 turbo bolts right into a 74 and later pinto.  The pinto suspension and brakes aren't gonna safely handle those speeds though-more $ for aftermarket stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000013||JohnnyK||12-20-2000||01:40 PM||||I've had my fun with refined engines. Now i want something that is about 429CI and cranking out over 400hp. The only things I am considering are 69-72 Mach1 mustangs, Chargers, Mustang Fastbacks, and 80's 5.0's. I'd rather have a Mach1 though. I heard that the Mach1s were the fastest mustangs? Can I get a 5.0 going as fast? i want to be able to hit 160-170 mph (no, it's not unrealistic) without taking days. I assume the Mach's could do this? What about a 5.0. Can you put a 429 in a 5.0?||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||12-20-2000||02:50 PM||||I like the mustang with a big block idea.  You'd have to beef up the suspension to drag around the extra weight though.  If the gearing is right, a big block with haul you fast enough to scare you. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gears5.gif"> I've always liked Mustangs since my dad had a 66 fastback w/5spd, a 691/2? GT350 Shelby, and a 68? GT500 Shelby when I was a little kid.  Too bad he sold them when I was too young.||||reg||1
Z||000015||JohnnyK||12-20-2000||03:45 PM||||GT500.. Damn thats a rare car. I think there were only about 2500 of them made? You like the classic mustang with the big block, or the 80's mustang with the big block?||||reg||1
Z||000016||1FST2M6||12-20-2000||03:49 PM||||the HP # from a 7MGTE (Supra Turbo)  The 323 GTX, Miata, and Mercury Capri Turbo (91-94) all have the same motor minus the turbo in the miata. the mercury turbo is a KILLER turbo toy.. running only 7.5psi lays down like 150.. add a $300 boost controller and you'll be laying 250hp! the dyno sheet above has stock (with a cat back and K&N) verses a  HKS boost controller and 3" down pipe about $750 in extra parts all installed in one day.   as for the older muscle cars.. if your wanting only to do parking lot and rolling (45mph) burn outs jump on them... if you want somthing that hooks up and is drivable, stick with a Fox body mustang.. sorry.. they are just TOO easy to make fast!! <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cheever2||12-20-2000||07:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>i want to be able to hit 160-170 mph </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> I was going to offer my humble advice, but it wouldn't come close to what you're wanting.  Buddy, that kind of speed is NOT going to come cheap, and won't even be dependable, as it will always need some work.  Besides, we're not the ones to ask when it comes to speed, are we?  Not that degree of speed anyway.  Good luck.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||WampusCat||12-20-2000||07:22 PM||||If you want 170mph cheap, buy a used Kawasaki ZX-11.  Bone stock it goes over 170mph with plenty of aftermarket mods available.  Yeah, it's dangerous, but so is going that fast in a 30 year old muscle car.||||reg||1
Z||000019||gixxer||12-20-2000||07:38 PM||||After reading most of the above threads, I've come away disgusted and a little disappointed.<BR>Imagine an '84-'88 Fiero with a nice 350HP Chevy engine wedged into it with some modern tires and shocks. <BR>Think about the top speed; 165+<BR>Think about the acceleration out of low and medium speed corners, considering that it will put the power to the ground better than about anything else out there because of it's mid-engined layout and rear weight bias.<BR>Think about what this package will do to about any other sports car on a twisty road.<BR>Think about the cost, maybe $10K-$15K.<BR>You guys have the raw material to make this happen, and you don't even realize it. Shame.(Tsk,Tsk) <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Cheever2||12-20-2000||07:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gixxer:<BR><B>Imagine an '84-'88 Fiero with a nice 350HP Chevy engine wedged into it...Think about the top speed; 165+...Think about the acceleration...Think about what this package will do...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>You can get all that AND good looks from Archie's Purple Pavement Eater (if it's still for sale), right?  Shuh, if I had the do-re-me I woulda snapped that up a long time ago.<P>||||reg||1
